From a1272f00e7e737de9b822e703d02054be2cd6243 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:27:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 090/110] media: i2c: s5k4ecgx: user adjustments at this
 firmware's addresses

The brightness, contrast and saturation controls wrote 0x7000022c,
0x7000022e and 0x70000230, the addresses of the old mainline driver.
With the firmware and tuning of the gtelwifi they are one word off: the
stock camera HAL's contrast and saturation tables write 0x70000232 and
0x70000234, and writing 0x70000230 changes the luma, not the chroma.
Measured while streaming: 0x70000230 from -127 to 127 moved the mean
luma from 50 to 120 with the chroma unchanged, 0x70000234 at -127, 0
and 127 gave a 99th-percentile chroma of 3, 7 and 14 with the luma
unchanged.

Use 0x70000230/232/234 and limit brightness to the signed range the
other two use.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 drivers/media/i2c/s5k4ecgx.c | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k4ecgx.c b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k4ecgx.c
index 551858cf9..991727baf 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k4ecgx.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k4ecgx.c
@@ -49,10 +49,15 @@
 #define S5K_FW_REVISION		0x700001a6
 #define S5K_G_ENABLE_PREV	0x7000023e
 #define S5K_G_ENABLE_PREV_CHG	0x70000240
-/* user adjustments on top of the tuning, signed, 0 = unchanged */
-#define S5K_USER_BRIGHTNESS	0x7000022c
-#define S5K_USER_CONTRAST	0x7000022e
-#define S5K_USER_SATURATION	0x70000230
+/*
+ * User adjustments on top of the tuning, signed, 0 = unchanged. Addresses
+ * as the stock HAL's contrast/saturation tables write them (and measured:
+ * 0x230 moves the luma, 0x234 the chroma); the old mainline driver's
+ * 0x22c/0x22e/0x230 are one word off for this firmware.
+ */
+#define S5K_USER_BRIGHTNESS	0x70000230
+#define S5K_USER_CONTRAST	0x70000232
+#define S5K_USER_SATURATION	0x70000234
 #define S5K_SATURATION_DEF	0
 
 #define S5K_MCLK_HZ		24000000
@@ -453,7 +458,7 @@ static int s5k_init_controls(struct s5k4ecgx *s5k)
 
 	v4l2_ctrl_handler_init(hdl, 7);
 	v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, &s5k_ctrl_ops, V4L2_CID_BRIGHTNESS,
-			  -208, 127, 1, 0);
+			  -127, 127, 1, 0);
 	v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, &s5k_ctrl_ops, V4L2_CID_CONTRAST,
 			  -127, 127, 1, 0);
 	v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, &s5k_ctrl_ops, V4L2_CID_SATURATION,
